+# Fix lower-case SKU entry, delivery threshold, and line VAT rounding
+
+Three reports about the order service this week, each checked against the business rules in `README.md`.
+
+## 1. Lower-case SKU is refused (Giulia, sales desk)
+
+Keying a product code in lower case, e.g. `lb-220`, is refused as an unknown product; the same code in
+capitals works.
+
+- Rule: SKUs are case-insensitive and ignore surrounding spaces; the service always shows a SKU in upper case.
+- Cause: `Catalog.find` (`src/catalog.ts`) trims the SKU but does not upper-case it, so it misses the
+  stored canonical SKU. `canonicalSku` already does both.
+- Fix: look products up by their canonical SKU.
+
+## 2. Delivery charged at €50.00 (Marco, customer)
+
+A basket of €50.00 after discount was charged €4.90 delivery; the website says delivery is free from €50.
+
+- Rule: shipping is free when the goods come to €50.00 or more, after every discount and before VAT.
+- Cause: `shippingCost` (`src/shipping.ts`) tests `goods > FREE_SHIPPING_FROM_CENTS`, which excludes exactly €50.00.
+- Fix: free shipping at `goods >= FREE_SHIPPING_FROM_CENTS`.
+
+## 3. Line VAT one cent low (accounting)
+
+A single €1.99 item at the standard rate shows €0.43 VAT on its line; accounting expects €0.44.
+
+- Rule: VAT is computed line by line on the line's net amount, rounded half up to the cent on each line.
+- Cause: `lineVat` (`src/tax.ts`) uses `Math.floor`, so 199 × 22 / 100 = 43.78 becomes 43 instead of 44.
+- Fix: round half up with `percentOf` / `divideHalfUp` from `src/money.ts`.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- Each of the three cases above has a test that fails before the fix and passes after it.
+- `npm test` passes in full.
+- Nothing else in the public behaviour changes; the change stays within the three functions named above.
